<h1>ANACONDA - Privacy Policy</h1>
<p><strong>Last updated:</strong> November 17, 2026</p>

<h2>1. Introduction</h2>
<p>
This Privacy Policy explains how ANACONDA, developed by panoramixIdeas,
handles information when you use the game. ANACONDA is intended for a
general audience, including children, teenagers and adults.
</p>

<h2>2. Information We Process</h2>

<h3>Firebase Authentication</h3>
<p>
ANACONDA uses Firebase Authentication to create anonymous player accounts.
A unique account identifier is generated to recognize your account and
associate it with your game data.
</p>

<h3>Firebase Firestore</h3>
<p>
If you use the online leaderboard, the game may store your chosen nickname,
anonymous account identifier, scores and completion times.
</p>

<h3>Firebase Analytics</h3>
<p>
Firebase Analytics may automatically collect usage and technical information,
such as app interactions, device information, app version and diagnostic
or usage events. This information helps us understand how the game is used
and improve its functionality.
</p>

<h3>Google AdMob</h3>
<p>
ANACONDA uses Google AdMob to display advertisements. Depending on applicable
settings and consent choices, Google and its advertising partners may process
information such as device identifiers, IP address, advertising interactions
and information used to deliver, limit or measure advertisements.
</p>

<h3>Google User Messaging Platform (UMP)</h3>
<p>
Google UMP is used to present applicable privacy and advertising consent
choices to users.
</p>

<h3>Local Storage</h3>
<p>
The game uses Android DataStore to save game progress and best completion
times locally on your device.
</p>

<h2>3. How Information Is Used</h2>
<p>Information is processed to:
</p>
<ul>
    <li>Provide anonymous player accounts.</li>
    <li>Save and display leaderboard results.</li>
    <li>Store game progress and completion times.</li>
    <li>Understand game usage and improve performance.</li>
    <li>Display and measure advertisements.</li>
</ul>

<h2>4. Third-Party Services</h2>
<p>ANACONDA uses the following Google services:</p>
<ul>
    <li>Firebase Authentication</li>
    <li>Firebase Cloud Firestore</li>
    <li>Firebase Analytics</li>
    <li>Google AdMob</li>
    <li>Google User Messaging Platform (UMP)</li>
</ul>
<p>
These services may process information according to their own privacy
policies and terms.
</p>
<p>
Google Privacy Policy:
<a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">
https://policies.google.com/privacy</a>
</p>

<h2>5. Children's Privacy</h2>
<p>
ANACONDA is intended for users of all ages, including children and teenagers.
We aim to comply with applicable child privacy and advertising requirements.
Where required, appropriate advertising settings and consent mechanisms
must be applied to protect younger users.
</p>
<p>
The game does not ask children to provide personal contact information
to play.
</p>

<h2>6. Sharing of Information</h2>
<p>
We do not sell personal information. Information may be processed by the
Google services listed in this policy to provide authentication, leaderboard,
analytics and advertising features.
</p>

<h2>7. Data Retention and Deletion</h2>
<p>
Game progress stored locally can be removed by clearing the app's data
or uninstalling the game.
</p>
<p>
Information associated with anonymous accounts and leaderboard entries
may remain stored in Firebase until deleted. To request deletion of
information associated with your account, contact us at the email below.
</p>

<h2>8. Data Security</h2>
<p>
We rely on the security features of the services we use and take reasonable
steps to protect information. However, no method of electronic storage
or transmission is completely secure.
</p>

<h2>9. Changes to This Policy</h2>
<p>
This Privacy Policy may be updated when the game, its services or applicable
requirements change. The latest version will be published on this page.
</p>

